cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite both the dataset and the tool that
  produced it (see CITATION.cff at the repository root).
type: dataset
title: "Civic-Tech Corpus — 2026-06 Refresh (n = 55, with AI-usage detection)"
abstract: >-
  A curated corpus of 55 open-source civic-technology repositories from 23
  organisations across five continents (North America, Africa, Japan, Taiwan,
  Europe), re-crawled 2026-06-03 to 2026-06-04. It extends the 2026-05 refresh
  with an AI-usage detection layer that distinguishes three phenomena:
  traditional/classical ML, LLMs shipped as a product feature, and LLM coding
  tools used to build the software (detected from agent config files, commit
  co-author trailers, AI agent-bot commits/PRs, CI agents, and review bots),
  each with first-appearance dating. Each repository also carries
  repository-level metrics, per-(repository, contributor) commit counts with a
  heuristic bot flag, PR and tag/release cadence, full-history weekly snapshots,
  per-(contributor, ISO-week) activity (commits + lines added/removed), 45+
  CHAOSS metrics including bus factor, elephant factor, HHI, and burstiness, and
  issue analytics. Companion analyses (statistical_analysis/,
  weekly_activity_analysis/, ai_usage_analysis/), figures, per-repository
  folders, and the pre-crawl candidate-selection list are included.
